==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Doguemon''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Reborn Warrior Doguemon''' at level 30 using [[Catfruit|Behemoth Stones]] and XP after completing [[Atonement for Sin]].

==Strategy/Usage==
Dogumaru is an [[:Category:Anti-Traitless Cats|anti-Traitless]] [[:Category:Tanker-class Cats|tanker]], a rare niche to behold. Otherwise, his points of interests are his fast movement speed, high attack power, low knockback count and cost, with added Warp/Curse Immunity to help against [[Mystic Mask Yulala]] and [[Master Uril (Enemy)|Master Uril]] respectively, though using him against Uril may be questionable as he'll cause Uril to set off more Surges and be killed by them quickly, as well as any stages pairing [[:Category:Traitless Enemies|Traitless]] enemies with the [[Relic Doge Base (Enemy Base)|Relic Doge Base]]. However, his recharge time is somewhat long for what he does, and he will struggle to counter enemies like [[Henry]] or [[Croakley]], who will render him useless if spawned at the wrong time. Lastly, he also excels at tanking isolated [[Dolphina]]s.

==='''True Form'''===
Reborn Warrior Doguemon's biggest improvements are a decent boost to HP, a recharge time reduction and Relic targeting, thus improving his existing niche and giving him a new niche against another trait.

His viability against Relic enemies is a mixed bag. On the one hand, his impressive HP and recharge time work against certain Relics, such as [[Spiritual Yulala (Enemy)|Spiritual Yulala]], [[Lowkey]] and even [[Dogumaru (Enemy)|Dogumaru]]. However, his lack of other immunities means that he does not do nearly as well against [[M. Ost]] and [[Masked Grandmaster Cat (Enemy)|Masked Grandmaster Cat]], for example, as he still gets chipped by [[Wave Attack|Waves]] or suffers from Knockback/Slow.

Additionally, this form grants Colossus Slayer and Behemoth Slayer, both of which can help quite well. Overlapping with his targeted traits, Reborn Warrior Doguemon's kit seems made especially for [[Wild Doge]], [[Elephantidae Papaou]] and [[Cumulus Gallus]], as well as [[Ultima Beast Naala]] on higher Crown difficulties, [[Iguanidae Ibilujon]], [[Ancient Magamojoe]], [[Great Ape Luza]] and [[Zero Luza]]. While Reborn Warrior Doguemon seems poised to take on these threats, his advantage is somewhat hindered by their tendency to fight alongside other enemies of many other traits (save for Zero Luza, whose [[Revival of Origin|stage]] solely consist of enemies within Reborn Warrior Doguemon's target traits). Additionally, Colossus Slayer does somewhat help against Colossus [[Gauntlet]]s in general, but those stages also have a variety of enemies to strike past Reborn Warrior Doguemon's abilities and exploit his lack of immunities, making him a subpar option. Still, Reborn Warrior Doguemon is overall a solid buff that improves his existing niche and works well in several more stages.

