==Trivia==
*Dogumaru is based on ''[[wikipedia:Dogū#Shakōkidogū|Shakōkidogū]]'', the most well-known variety of clay ''dogū'' figurines from prehistoric Japan.
**The word ''maru'' (丸) in Dogumaru's name can mean "full" or "whole" in Japanese. This may refer to how being attached to a horse statue's lower body (as mentioned in his [[Dogumaru (Enemy)|enemy counterpart]]'s description) has made Dogumaru complete again, as ''Shakōkidogū'' in real life are seldom found with all of their limbs intact.
*The term ''[[wikipedia:Haniwa|haniwa]]'' in his Evolved and True Forms' Japanese descriptions refers to a type of ancient clay figurine that used to be buried alongside the dead.
*Since the end of [[Uncanny Legends]] involves the [[Great Ape Luza|origin of humanity]], Dogumaru may represent myths of [[wikipedia:Creation of life from clay|creation of life from clay]], many of which state that the first human(s) were made from clay.
*For a few reasons, Dogumaru could potentially be a nod to [https://youtu.be/Ne4qy1MwVDo Hanimaru] from the children's television program [[wikipedia:ja:おーい!はに丸|''Ōi! Hanimaru'']]:
**Both combine the name of an ancient Japanese clay figurine with 丸 ''maru'' (Hanimaru is ''haniwa'', Dogumaru is ''dogū'').
**The Japanese descriptions of his Evolved and True Forms say that he is a ''haniwa''.
**Hanimaru is usually seen with his horse ''haniwa'' Hinbei, while the enemy Dogumaru's Japanese description states that he was mistakenly attached to the lower body of a horse ''dogū'' that had fallen beside him.
*The "cBay" in Dogumaru's description is a reference to the online marketplace [[wikipedia:eBay|eBay]].
*Dogumaru's attack animation is reminiscent of a [[wikia:zelda-archive:Guardian (Breath of the Wild)|Guardian]] from ''[[wikipedia:The Legend of Zelda: Breath of the Wild|The Legend of Zelda: Breath of the Wild]]'', locking on to his target with a red light before shooting an explosive blue beam.
*Doguemon is likely a reference to ''[[wikipedia:Doraemon|Doraemon]]'', the protagonist of the eponymous franchise, who is also a cat-like construct with a bell around his neck. Ironically, this bell is not passed over to Reborn Warrior Doguemon.
*Doguemon's stance resembles that of a ''[[wikipedia:Maneki-neko|maneki-neko]]'', a traditional Japanese figurine considered a symbol of good fortune and prosperity.
*Dogumaru is the first [[:Category:Mythic Cats|Mythic Cat]] whose stats change between his Normal and Evolved Forms, the second being [[Idi:N (Special Cat)|Idi:N]].
*Between [[Version 11.5 Update|Version 11.5]] and [[Version 12.0 Update|Version 12.0]], Dogumaru was the only Uncanny Legends drop unit who increased the player's [[Enigma Stages|Enigma]] Level.

